* ATmega48A/PA/88A/PA/168A/PA/328/P Pin Definitions -- 28-pin PDIP /
* 28-pad QFN/MLF package
* Source: Microchip DS40002061A "megaAVR Data Sheet
*         ATmega48A/PA/88A/PA/168A/PA/328/P", Figure 1-1 (Pinout,
*         28 PDIP and 28 MLF views) and Section 1.1 (Pin Descriptions).
*
* Primary device: ATmega328 (no "P" suffix) -- this determines the
* file name. The P record below keeps the datasheet's own listing
* order (48A/PA/88A/PA/168A/PA/328/P) rather than reordering around
* the primary device.
*
* Companion devices -- all eight family members share this exact
* 28-pin signal set. Per Table 2-1 (Memory Size Summary), they differ
* ONLY in Flash/EEPROM/SRAM size and interrupt-vector word size --
* never in pin count, pin names, or peripheral pin assignments:
*   ATmega48A, ATmega48PA, ATmega88A, ATmega88PA, ATmega168A,
*   ATmega168PA, ATmega328 (primary), ATmega328P
*
* Package scope -- this file covers the 28-pin package ONLY (PDIP and
* QFN/MLF). The same datasheet also documents a 32-pin TQFP/QFN/MLF
* package for this family, which is NOT pin-compatible with this file
* (it adds ADC6/ADC7 as dedicated analog-only pins with no 28-pin
* equivalent) and would need its own companion file.
*
* Per this project's established principle, physical pin numbers are
* not part of the .qpindef format. This matters here specifically:
* the 28-PDIP and 28-QFN/MLF packages use CONFLICTING physical pin
* numbering schemes for the identical signal set (PDIP numbers 1-28
* around two long edges; QFN/MLF numbers 1-28 around a 7x7 square).
* Since numbering is irrelevant to this format, both packages are
* covered by this single file without conflict. The QFN/MLF package
* additionally has an exposed thermal pad on the bottom that should
* be soldered to ground -- not a distinct signal, no separate record
* needed (already covered by the G record below).
*
* Flagged for manual review (dual-function / non-obvious pins):
*   PC6/RESET -- classic fuse-selectable dual-function pin. Default
*              (RSTDISBL fuse unprogrammed) is dedicated active-low
*              Reset input. If RSTDISBL is programmed, PC6 becomes a
*              GPIO pin -- but the datasheet explicitly states it is
*              "used as an I/O pin" in that mode with electrical
*              characteristics differing from the rest of Port C.
*              Classified I here (not B) per this project's
*              established convention for this exact pin on other
*              family members (matches yesterday's ATmega328P
*              automotive-32-pin treatment).
*   PB6, PB7 -- oscillator-mode-dependent, on top of their normal GPIO
*              function (XTAL1/XTAL2 or TOSC1/TOSC2 depending on
*              clock-selection fuse settings). Classified B for their
*              default GPIO role.
*   AVCC     -- separate ANALOG power rail. Datasheet: "It should be
*              externally connected to VCC, even if the ADC is not
*              used." Same voltage in practice, architecturally
*              separate pin/rail -- recorded as I per this project's
*              established workaround.
*   AREF     -- external ADC voltage reference input; dedicated, not
*              multiplexed with any GPIO port bit.
*
* No ADC6/ADC7 on this package -- datasheet explicitly scopes those
* two dedicated analog-input pins to "TQFP and QFN/MLF Package Only"
* (i.e. the 32-pin variant), so they are correctly absent here.
*
* VCC occupies one physical pin on both packages; GND occupies two
* physical pins on both packages (plus the QFN/MLF thermal pad, not
* separately counted). Same net regardless of physical pin count;
* one V and one G record cover them.

D ATmega48A/PA/88A/PA/168A/PA/328/P 28-Pin PDIP/QFN/MLF 8-bit AVR Microcontroller Family
P ATmega48A ATmega48PA ATmega88A ATmega88PA ATmega168A ATmega168PA ATmega328 ATmega328P

V VCC
I AREF
I AVCC
B PB0 PCINT0/CLKO/ICP1
B PB1 PCINT1/OC1A
B PB2 PCINT2/SS/OC1B
B PB3 PCINT3/OC2A/MOSI
B PB4 PCINT4/MISO
B PB5 SCK/PCINT5
B PB6 PCINT6/XTAL1/TOSC1
B PB7 PCINT7/XTAL2/TOSC2
B PC0 ADC0/PCINT8
B PC1 ADC1/PCINT9
K SIMCLK

B PC2 ADC2/PCINT10
B PC3 ADC3/PCINT11
B PC4 ADC4/SDA/PCINT12
B PC5 ADC5/SCL/PCINT13
I PC6 RESET/PCINT14
B PD0 RXD/PCINT16
B PD1 TXD/PCINT17
B PD2 INT0/PCINT18
B PD3 PCINT19/OC2B/INT1
B PD4 PCINT20/XCK/T0
B PD5 PCINT21/OC0B/T1
B PD6 PCINT22/OC0A/AIN0
B PD7 PCINT23/AIN1
G GND
